diff --git a/HEGEL_REPORT.md b/HEGEL_REPORT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1d187b8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/HEGEL_REPORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,165 @@
+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report: `tiff`
+
+## 1. Scope and Approach
+
+Property-based tests (hegel, `cargo add --dev hegeltest`) were added for the
+TIFF decoder and encoder, targeting the crate's primary threat model: the
+decoder consumes fully untrusted input, where IFD tag tables carry
+attacker-controlled dimensions, strip offsets/byte-counts, tag counts and
+value offsets.
+
+The existing fuzz target (`fuzz/fuzz_targets/decode_comprehensive.rs`) was
+read first and used as the template for how maintainers drive the decoder
+(directory walking, tag iteration, chunk + full-image reads, capped
+`Limits`). The properties supplement it with things libFuzzer does not give:
+structured adversarial IFDs with field-level sane/adversarial mixing,
+valid-then-corrupt mutation of encoder output, an encode→decode pixel-exact
+roundtrip across the configuration space, and a spec-transcribed byte-order
+oracle. Tests were added to the existing test files, not new ones:
+
+- `tests/fuzz_tests.rs` — decoder robustness properties (mod `hegel_robustness`)
+- `tests/encode_images.rs` — encode→decode roundtrips (mod `hegel_roundtrip`)
+- `tests/decode_images.rs` — byte-order consistency (mod `hegel_decode`)
+
+## 2. Properties Added (7)
+
+1. **`decode_arbitrary_bytes_never_panics`** (fuzz_tests.rs) — arbitrary
+   bytes, optionally prefixed with valid `II*\0` / `MM\0*` / BigTIFF
+   (`II+\0`/`MM\0+`) magic and an IFD pointer, are driven through header
+   parse, directory walk, tag iteration, metadata queries, `read_chunk(0)`
+   and `read_image` under capped `Limits` (512 KiB buffers, 64 KiB IFD
+   values, mirroring the fuzz target). Every call may `Err`; none may panic,
+   hang, or allocate past the limits (an OOM abort would fail the run).
+
+2. **`crafted_ifd_fields_never_panic_or_oom`** (fuzz_tests.rs) — a
+   hand-serialized, syntactically well-formed classic TIFF (both byte
+   orders) whose nine core IFD fields (width, height, bits/sample,
+   compression, photometric, strip offset + count, samples/pixel,
+   rows/strip, strip byte count + count) are each independently sane or
+   adversarial (0, 1, `0xFFFF`, `0x7FFFFFFF`, `u32::MAX`, arbitrary; entry
+   counts up to `u32::MAX` turning value fields into external-array
+   offsets). A quarter of cases are fully sane, so the decode-success path
+   (strip reading, dimension-sanity assert) fires on every run — verified at
+   ~36 hits per 100 cases. This is the decompression-bomb/crafted-dimension
+   property: huge width×height or strip byte counts must not pre-allocate
+   before `Limits` are consulted.
+
+3. **`corrupted_valid_tiff_never_panics`** (fuzz_tests.rs) — a valid
+   encoder-produced Gray8 TIFF is truncated at an arbitrary point and/or has
+   up to 8 arbitrary bytes overwritten (header, IFD, offsets, pixel data all
+   reachable); decoding must not panic, and any *successful* decode must
+   satisfy the dimension-sanity invariant.
+
+   Properties 1–3 share a probe that, whenever `read_image` succeeds, checks
+   the **dimension-sanity invariant**: the buffer's element count equals the
+   count computed from decoder-reported dimensions, colortype and planar
+   configuration (`w*h*samples` for depths >= 8; row-padded packed bytes,
+   `planes * h * ceil(w*texel_samples*bits/8)`, for sub-byte depths).
+
+4. **`roundtrip_arbitrary_image_and_config`** (encode_images.rs, the crown
+   roundtrip) — draws dimensions (1–16 square), one of 15 color types
+   (Gray/GrayI 8/16/32/64, RGB8/16, RGBA8, CMYK8, Gray32Float, Gray64Float,
+   RGB32Float), compression (Uncompressed / LZW / Deflate level 1–9 /
+   Packbits), predictor (None / Horizontal for integer, None / FloatingPoint
+   for float samples), classic vs BigTIFF container, and an optional strip
+   size (including strips larger than the image); encodes drawn full-range
+   pixels (floats include NaN and infinities) and decodes them back,
+   asserting reported dimensions and bit-exact pixel recovery (`to_bits`
+   comparison for floats).
+
+5. **`multipage_roundtrip`** (encode_images.rs) — 1–4 Gray8 pages of drawn
+   sizes: `more_images`/`next_image` walks exactly the encoded pages in
+   order with exact pixels, and `seek_to_image` random access agrees with
+   the sequential walk.
+
+6. **`strip_chunks_reassemble_to_image`** (encode_images.rs) — for drawn
+   `rows_per_strip` (1..height+4; Packbits excluded since the encoder
+   documents row-per-strip packing for it): `strip_count == ceil(h /
+   rows_per_strip)`, per-strip `chunk_data_dimensions` tile the image height
+   exactly at full width, the concatenation of `read_chunk(i)` equals the
+   encoded pixels, and equals `read_image`.
+
+7. **`byte_order_ii_vs_mm_decode_identically`** (decode_images.rs) — a
+   spec-transcribed writer (independent of the crate's encoder, which only
+   emits native byte order) serializes the same drawn Gray16 image as both
+   `II` (little-endian) and `MM` (big-endian) TIFFs; both must decode to
+   exactly the source pixels with correct reported byte order, dimensions
+   and colortype.
+
+Plus one deliberately failing test pinning a bug (see section 3):
+**`rows_per_strip_returns_err_instead_of_panicking`** (encode_images.rs).
+
+## 3. Bugs Found
+
+**`ImageEncoder::rows_per_strip(0)` panics instead of returning `Err`.**
+`rows_per_strip` returns `TiffResult<()>` and its docs do not exclude any
+value, but passing `0` hits an unchecked division:
+`(self.height as u64).div_ceil(value)` at `src/encoder/mod.rs:895` —
+`attempt to divide by zero`. Pinned by the deterministically-failing test
+`hegel_roundtrip::rows_per_strip_returns_err_instead_of_panicking`
+(a `one_of!(just(0), ...)` branch guarantees the counterexample every run;
+hegel shrinks it to `width=1, height=1, rows=0`). Per instructions the bug
+was **not** fixed; this is the only failing test in the suite. Encoder-side,
+caller-triggered, not reachable from untrusted decode input — severity low,
+but it violates the function's own `TiffResult` contract.
+
+No decoder-side panic, OOM, hang, or invariant violation was found — at
+default counts, at 10x counts (1000 cases/property), and with the
+non-default `zstd-safe-rust` + `webp` decode features enabled. Consistent
+with a crate that ships a comprehensive fuzz target and a regression corpus
+(`tests/fuzz_images/`).
+
+One initially-failing property was a **test-model error, not a crate bug**:
+the dimension-sanity invariant assumed one buffer element per sample, but
+for sub-byte bit depths (e.g. a crafted `BitsPerSample = 1`) the decoder
+documents (comment in `readout_for_size`, `src/decoder/image.rs`) that
+samples stay packed, rows padded to byte boundaries. Found by the 10x run in
+both robustness properties (shrunk to a 2×1 1-bit image); the invariant was
+corrected to the actual layout contract and re-verified.
+
+## 4. Validation (Run and Reflect)
+
+- **Liveness**: three representative assertions were temporarily inverted —
+  the guarded dimension-sanity assert (fails, shrunk to a minimal 1×1 Gray8
+  crafted TIFF), the roundtrip length assert, and the byte-order pixel
+  assert (both fail, shrunk to 1×1 images) — then reverted and the `.hegel`
+  failure database cleared.
+- **Guard firing**: the decode-success branch containing the sanity assert
+  was counted: 36/100 cases in the crafted-IFD property (after restructuring
+  the generator to mix sane/adversarial fields; it was 0/100 with
+  all-adversarial fields), 11/100 in the corruption property. The
+  arbitrary-bytes property essentially never decodes successfully, as
+  expected; its assertion (no panic) does not live behind the guard.
+- **High-count exploratory run**: all seven properties were run at
+  `test_cases = 1000` (10x) with per-case counters confirming the case
+  counts (e.g. 1000/1082/1004/1166/1023 cases observed). This run found the
+  sub-byte packing modeling error described above; after the fix, all
+  properties pass at 1000 cases. Committed tests use the default count.
+- **Feature matrix**: the robustness properties were additionally run with
+  `--features zstd-safe-rust,webp` (non-default decode paths reachable via
+  crafted compression tags); green.
+- Full suite: `cargo test --no-fail-fast` — all 253 tests pass except the
+  single intentional known-failure pin.
+
+## 5. Limitations and Future Work
+
+- **Tiles are not generated**: the encoder only writes strips, and the
+  crafted-IFD generator does not emit TileWidth/TileLength/TileOffsets
+  layouts. Tile-specific arithmetic is exercised only when garbage/corrupted
+  inputs happen to contain tile tags. A tile-aware crafted generator is the
+  natural next property.
+- **JPEG/WebP/Zstd/Fax compressed data paths** are only reachable through
+  the crafted compression tag with garbage payloads (error paths), since the
+  encoder cannot produce them; deep decode paths of those codecs are covered
+  by their own crates.
+- **BigTIFF adversarial IFDs**: crafted IFDs are classic TIFF (BigTIFF is
+  covered on the roundtrip side and via magic-prefixed garbage); a BigTIFF
+  variant of the crafted-IFD builder (8-byte counts/offsets, e.g.
+  `u64::MAX` entry counts) would extend the bomb coverage.
+- **Memory/time bounds are indirect**: OOM/hang detection relies on the
+  process aborting or the suite visibly stalling under capped `Limits`;
+  there is no per-test rusage assertion.
+- The dimension-sanity invariant intentionally re-derives the documented
+  layout contract from independently queried metadata; it would not catch a
+  bug where dimensions, colortype *and* buffer size are all consistently
+  wrong together.
